# Rules to skip for specific paths in this crate.
# Format: RULE/name:path/glob — gitignore-style glob relative to crate root.
# Every entry requires a WHY: comment. No blanket category ignores.

# WHY: kerykeion is a library crate. Items declared `pub` inside src/*.rs are
# surface of the crate's external API — they are re-exported from `lib.rs`
# via `pub use` and consumed by sibling crates (`akroasis`, `semaino`) and
# downstream users. Downgrading to `pub(crate)` breaks `pub use` re-exports
# (Rust E0365/E0624). Methods on re-exported types are likewise part of
# that public surface. Bare `pub` is correct here; the RUST/pub-visibility
# rule's exemption for lib.rs/mod.rs does not extend to the item-definition
# files those `pub use` statements point at.
RUST/pub-visibility:src/**
